---
/*
  FilterField — the box that shortens a list, and the line that says nothing
  matched.

  ⚠ IT WRAPS THE LIST RATHER THAN SITTING BESIDE IT, and that is the whole
  design. The no-match line has to render AFTER the rows, so a component that
  emitted only the field would leave every caller hand-writing its own `<p>` —
  which is exactly the duplication this replaces. The rows go in the slot; the
  field, the rows and the line are then one owner (plan 42 · §4.B.2).

  ⚠ FOUR CALL SITES HAD FOUR ANSWERS AND ONLY ONE OF THEM WAS COMPLETE.
  `ConstellationPicker` had a no-match line and a threshold that re-checks
  itself; `SharedByField`, `EventSheet` and `TagSheet` shared a SIX-LINE PASS
  COPIED VERBATIM THREE TIMES with no no-match line at all — so on those three,
  filtering to nothing showed an empty box and no explanation. The complete one
  won and the other three gained the line.

  ⚠ THE CHROME IS `.search`, NOT `input-xs `. Both existed: four
  fields were the bare daisyUI input, four were `.search` + `ph:magnifying-glass`
  (the roster, `MergeDialog`, `LinkSheet`, `FragmentListPanel`). `.search` wins
  because it carries the magnifier — R16 standardises one glyph per affordance,
  and a search box whose only cue is a placeholder loses that cue the moment you
  type in it. `.search--w` is what stops hq.css's fixed `9rem` from stranding
  the field at a third of a drawer.

  ⚠ NOT `autocomplete="off"`, DELIBERATELY — and it is the opposite of what the
  neighbouring fields do. `MergeDialog` and `WritingSheet` both switch restore
  off. Here the browser SHOULD restore the query, because `wireFilterField`
  re-applies from the field's own value on wire: the surfaces this mounts on
  reload after a save (ADR 0036), and on a page whose job is *filter to the row,
  then groom it* a filter destroyed by the save is worse than no filter. Restore
  without the re-apply is the live defect on `/admin/people` — the text comes
  back, `input` never fires, and a filled box sits over an unfiltered list.

  ⚠ NOT USED BY: the roster, Notes' file picker, `MergeDialog`, the fragment
  panel, `LinkSheet` — and each refusal is specific, not an oversight. The
  roster also hides section headings and rewrites counts; Notes' picker and
  `MergeDialog` fetch; the fragment panel is a server GET (`name="q"`), not a
  DOM pass at all; and `LinkSheet` runs ONE field over TWO swappable lists with
  a no-match line in each, re-filtering on mode switch. Folding that last one in
  needs a two-list mode this would carry for a single caller — and `LinkSheet`
  already renders this exact chrome by hand, so the axis this component exists
  to settle is already settled there.
*/
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import { FILTER_THRESHOLD } from '../../lib/filtering';

interface Props {
  /** How many rows the slot holds — read against `threshold`, not counted from the DOM. */
  count: number;
  /** Selector, within this wrapper, for the rows that hide and show. They carry `data-search`. */
  rows: string;
  /**
   * Optional selector for a CONTAINER that hides when it holds no visible row —
   * a section with its own heading, so a filter cannot leave a heading standing
   * over an empty table. The roster wrote this rule first, in its own words: *"a
   * heading over an empty grid reads as a rendering bug."*
   */
  groups?: string;
  placeholder: string;
  /** The field's accessible name. It has no visible label; this is the only one it gets. */
  label: string;
  /** Shown only when a query matches nothing — never over an empty list. */
  noMatch?: string;
  /** Rows below which the field stays hidden. `null` always shows it. */
  threshold?: number | null;
  class?: string;
  /** Spacing for the field itself; the wrapper owns none, so callers keep their own rhythm. */
  fieldClass?: string;
}
const {
  count,
  rows,
  groups,
  placeholder,
  label,
  noMatch = 'Nothing matches.',
  threshold = FILTER_THRESHOLD,
  class: className = '',
  fieldClass = 'mb-1.5',
} = Astro.props;
---

{
  /* The field is RENDERED ALWAYS and hidden below the threshold, rather than
    branched away — `ConstellationPicker`'s reasoning, kept because it is right
    for all four: creating a constellation from the picker's own footer can push
    the sky past 8 mid-session, and a filter that only arrives on the next page
    load is a filter you learn not to expect. `sync()` re-checks it. */
}
<div class:list={['ff', className]} data-ff data-rows={rows} data-groups={groups} data-threshold={threshold ?? ''}>
  <label class:list={['search search--w', fieldClass]} hidden={threshold !== null && count <= threshold}>
    <Icon name="ph:magnifying-glass" class="shrink-0 opacity-45" />
    <input type="search" placeholder={placeholder} aria-label={label} />
  </label>
  <slot />
  <p class="ff__none admin-hint mt-1" hidden>{noMatch}</p>
</div>
